## Context: Counts successfully resolved vanilla default permutations; no-tag and candidate-filter coverage gaps are different. Unresolved IDs are logged separately, not counted as untagged. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
lothlorien.message.probe.tags_done=Vanilla block defaults: checked %s; without tags %s; outside candidate filter %s. Details in the Content Log.
## Context: The rig did not establish a required piston movement, so no support behavior verdict is possible. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
lothlorien.message.probe.inconclusive=inconclusive; check the rig in the Content Log
## Context: Count of cases excluded from pass/fail conclusions because the rig did not perform the required movement. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
lothlorien.message.probe.inconclusive_count=Inconclusive support tests: %s.
## Context: Announces a reserved empty test rig area and asks the operator to keep it loaded. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
lothlorien.message.probe.started=Support test started at %s. Stay nearby and keep the rig clear. About two minutes.
## Context: Summary of saved or newly completed native engine cases. Inconclusive cases are separate from actual failures. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
lothlorien.message.probe.summary=Support tests: passed %s; failed %s; inconclusive %s; total %s.
## Context: Groups each variant’s six-face, four-cause support-loss matrix into one line; individual movement cases remain separate. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
lothlorien.message.probe.group=%s: passed %s; failed %s; inconclusive %s.
## Context: Optional full case listing command; both report commands re-emit saved verdicts and failure reasons to the Creator Log. Temporary native support/piston experiment; remove after review.
